  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 2♠. The defense takes 3 heart tricks and switches to a club. As the ♦A is a sure loser, it appears that South must either successfully finesse in clubs or find the ♦J to make the contract. South can play either opponent for the ♦J.\n\nSouth can guarantee his contract by playing for an elimination. South should win the ♣A and draw trump. South now exits the ♣Q endplaying whichever defender wins the ♣K. A diamond return will pick up the ♦J regardless of its location. A heart or club return will be equally helpful, providing a ruff and discard.",
